{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And make one cherub from the end.</b> Lest you say two cherubim for each and every end — therefore it was necessary to specify ״כְּרוּב אֶחָד מִקָּצָה מִזֶּה״." "<b>From the cover.</b> Make the cherubim out of it itself — this is the meaning of ״מִקְשָׁה תַּעֲשֶׂה אוֹתָם״: do not make them on their own and then attach them to the cover."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:29.107318631Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}